1|# Design: task 4 Oz pipeline (Standard model)
2|
3|Goal: ingest the Oz text, split chapters into scenes with Meta, classify each scene with Jev plus a Meta override on low confidence, and cluster scene vectors into about 15 music track prompts. Branch `pipeline-oz`. The Next.js skeleton lands on another branch, so this task touches only `core/`, `pipeline/`, `data/books/oz/`, tests, docs, and the listed config changes.
4|
5|Binding inputs: AGENTS.md (project and Lectoria rules), SECURITY.md. There is no `docs/product-rules.md`; AGENTS.md carries the product rules. The raw text lives at `data/raw/oz/pg55.txt` (gitignored, CRLF, 24 chapters numbered I through XXIV, confirmed by heading scan).
6|
7|## Module layout
8|
9|```text
10|core/
11|  types.ts          book, chapter, paragraph, scene, emotion, provenance types, EMOTIONS
12|  gutenberg.ts      strip header/footer, split paragraphs, assign ids and ordinals
13|  scenes.ts         scene coverage validators (single chapter, whole book)
14|  emotion.ts        override decision, renormalization, final assembly
15|  cluster.ts        deterministic k-means over scene features
16|  music-prompt.ts   base template plus per cluster mood, dynamics, BPM
17|pipeline/
18|  books.json        per book config (gutenberg id, title, author)
19|  http.ts           fetchWithRetry plus a small concurrency pool (no dep)
20|  meta.ts           Meta chat client (OpenAI compatible body, usage parse)
21|  jev.ts            Jev client (state and questions builder lives here, not core)
22|  prices.ts         one price table and cost helpers (Jev, Meta, totals)
23|  cache.ts          skip if output exists with same textVersion, unless force
24|  ingest.ts         read raw or download, call core, freeze check, write book.json
25|  segment.ts        one Meta call per chapter, validate, retry once, write scenes.json
26|  classify.ts       one Jev call per scene, override path, write analysis.json
27|  cluster-tracks.ts feature build, k-means, prompts, write music-clusters.json
28|  build.ts          CLI entry: args, env load, step order, summary print
29|```
30|
31|`core/` exports pure functions and types only. `pipeline/` reads env, files, and network, and passes clients into orchestration functions as arguments so tests inject fakes.
32|
33|## Core types and signatures
34|
35|`core/types.ts` holds every shared shape. `EMOTIONS` is the single source: `export const EMOTIONS = [...] as const` with the 8 ids in AGENTS.md order, and `export type EmotionId = (typeof EMOTIONS)[number]`. Jev ids add `unknown`: `export type JevEmotionId = EmotionId | "unknown"`.
36|
37|```ts
38|// Branded ordinals keep n apart from chapter numbers.
39|export interface Book { id: string; title: string; author: string;
40|  source: { gutenberg: number; url: string }; textVersion: string;
41|  chapters: Chapter[]; paragraphs: Paragraph[]; }
42|export interface Chapter { ch: number; title: string; start_n: number; end_n: number; }
43|export interface Paragraph { id: string; ch: number; n: number; text: string; }
44|export interface SceneInput { start_n: number; end_n: number; title: string;
45|  summary: string; characters: string[]; }
46|export interface Scene extends SceneInput { id: string; ch: number; }
