191|## Open choices decided
192|
193|- Hash in `pipeline` with `node:crypto` over `core.canonicalLines`, because that keeps core free of node imports with no extra plumbing.
194|- One `pipeline/http.ts` for retry plus pool, because segment and classify need the same policy and one copy is easier to test.
195|- One `pipeline/meta.ts` client shared by segment and classify, because the endpoint, auth, and usage parsing are identical.
196|- `capSceneText` keeps the first 6000 and last 6000 chars with a marker, because scene openings and endings carry the mood shift.
197|- BPM maps tempo linearly to 60 through 160 (`round(60 + tempo * 100)`, range plus or minus 10), because picture book scoring stays inside a playable acoustic range.
198|- `pipeline/cache.ts` owns the skip if fresh check, because three steps share it and the freeze rule stays in one place.
199|- Prices live in `pipeline/prices.ts` as plain constants, because costs are pipeline reporting, not domain logic.
